<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ode to the Motherland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a>; published <a href="/years/1951">1951</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 歌唱祖国, Gēchàng Zǔguó</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Ode to the Motherland&quot; is a patriotic song of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>, with words and music by Wang Shen (1918–2007), a musician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tianjin">Tianjin</a>. In late September 1950, on a work trip to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a>, he passed through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Tiananmen</a> Square as people prepared for National Day on 1 October, the first anniversary of the People's Republic, and was moved by the festive sea of flags; he wrote a first draft on the train back to Tianjin.</p></div>
